  "completed": [
    "A numeric child PID is accepted only once at the immediate post-fork pidfd_open boundary; every later liveness, signal, wait and close operation is bound to the resulting generation-stable pidfd.",
    "The private binder admits exactly one non-inheritable pidfd with a stable fdinfo identity, a fixed guardian, broker or worker role, one process/thread owner and one absolute deadline.",
    "Initial admission proves the child has not already exited through non-consuming waitid(P_PIDFD) plus a zero-time pidfd readiness check. A child already exited during admission is terminated only if needed, consumed, reaped and closed before the original fixed failure is returned.",
    "Termination is one-shot and uses pidfd_send_signal(SIGKILL) only. ProcessLookupError is treated only as a possible race and never as proof of exit; a real waitid observation and consuming reap remain mandatory.",
    "Reap requires pidfd readiness before two matching waitid events: WEXITED|WNOHANG|WNOWAIT followed by WEXITED|WNOHANG. Only the exact bound child identity and a valid exited, killed or dumped event are accepted.",
    "Successful exit means CLD_EXITED with status zero. Nonzero or signaled exit may be reaped for cleanup but cannot satisfy a success-required call.",
    "Pidfd close is permitted only after reap. It consumes the close attempt before the final descriptor-identity check, never closes a replacement descriptor and never retries an ambiguous close.",
    "All public entry paths remain closed. Snapshots retain only role and aggregate state, with no PID, pidfd, fdinfo identity, exit event detail or exception text."
  ],
  "fixed_lifecycle": {
    "roles": [
      "guardian",
      "broker",
      "worker"
    ],
    "pidfd_open_attempts_per_binding": 1,
