  "remaining_integration_work": [
    "Implement the actual private fork composition over the frozen six-pair topology: outer controller creates and pidfd-binds guardian; guardian adopts its prefork copy, creates the cgroup lease, then creates and pidfd-binds broker and worker; each child transitions to its exact final descriptor set.",
    "Implement one controller event loop over control, ledger, broker-report and worker-report endpoints, including READY verification before guardian arm, aggregate reservation before each CONTINUE, CONSUMED verification, terminal reports and deadline cleanup through these pidfd owners.",
    "Integrate listener handoff and adoption, worker privilege drop and final seal, guardian-v2 authority consumption, full-size bootstrap and entry, and authenticated source closure.",
    "Run a separately authorized bounded Linux native qualification of fork, topology, pidfd, waitid, signal, cgroup and socket semantics before any real checkpoint payload read or import.",
    "Re-run unchanged host, input, resource and real-import admission only after native qualification succeeds."
  ],
